{"type":"assistant","message":{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The issue was in `round_to_nickel` in `repo/pricing.py`. Report totals use that helper via `price_summary` in `rows.py`, which sums each line after nickel rounding.\n\nThe implementation used integer floor division (`(cents // 5) * 5`), so amounts always dropped to the lower nickel. For example, 23¢ became 20¢ instead of 25¢, which made rounded totals in the report look systematically low.\n\nIt now uses nearest-nickel rounding: `round(cents / 5) * 5`, matching the docstring (23 → 25, 22 → 20). All pricing tests pass."}]},"session_id":"df3c2bf2-4498-41d4-8034-5d711e459f83"}
{"type":"result","subtype":"success","duration_ms":24430,"duration_api_ms":24430,"is_error":false,"result":"Searching the codebase for how report prices are rounded.\n\n\nIdentifying the bug: `round_to_nickel` floors to the lower nickel instead of rounding to the nearest (e.g. 23¢ → 20¢ instead of 25¢).\n\n\nThe issue was in `round_to_nickel` in `repo/pricing.py`. Report totals use that helper via `price_summary` in `rows.py`, which sums each line after nickel rounding.\n\nThe implementation used integer floor division (`(cents // 5) * 5`), so amounts always dropped to the lower nickel. For example, 23¢ became 20¢ instead of 25¢, which made rounded totals in the report look systematically low.\n\nIt now uses nearest-nickel rounding: `round(cents / 5) * 5`, matching the docstring (23 → 25, 22 → 20). All pricing tests pass.","session_id":"df3c2bf2-4498-41d4-8034-5d711e459f83","request_id":"9944d965-d9b1-4ceb-bba8-8d6b863679a4","usage":{"inputTokens":11151,"outputTokens":1383,"cacheReadTokens":59168,"cacheWriteTokens":0}}
